in our Krewe was poisoned, so she can use poison on herself (more deadly dose=more Plasm). One that actually died of disease will take some thought.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always thought that for Forgotten it would be very situational. For example, my character died in a boating accident (hence my standing in a sinking canoe comment.) Gambling would not make much sense for her to do as far as fulfilling archetypes goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2152-phyi","name":"Phyi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2152_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T22:34:48-07:00","id":850973,"title":"","content":"Which is fair. Chance just seems closely tied. I guess it depends on how much you see the themes grating plasm vs. specific events. We have a Torn who was killed by an IED. I've still let him recover a little from gunfire. He would recover more from something closer to his death. Just how I do it, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-